{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>From the beginning of the year</b> — the letters of מתשרי: adjacent to \"the eyes of YHWH your Elohim are upon it\" is לוהיה, to say: if you will indeed hearken, \"the eyes of YHWH your Elohim are upon it,\" for as the face answers to face in water." "<b>And until the end of the year</b>"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The notarikon מתשרי expands to the phrase beginning with סמך עיני ה'; לוהיה appears to be a Masoretic notation indicating that ל follows ויה, though its precise function here is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:23.162941700Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}